    "id": 57,
    "sourceNumber": "58",
    "chapter": "Vīthisaṅgaha (Chapter 4) Day 1",
    "question": "How many tadanuvattikamanodvāravīthis after cakkhudvāravīthis are there? What are they? Write the sequence of those vīthis?",
    "answer": "There are 4 tadanuvattikamanodvāravīthis: 1.atītaggahaṇavīthi 2.samūhaggahaṇavīthi 3.atthaggahaṇavīthi 4.nāmaggahaṇavīthi The sequence of those vīthis are as follows: 1.After bhavaṅgacittas after cakkhudvāravīthi, atīta (past, previous) rūpārammaṇa appear in the mind, this cause atītaggahaṇavīthi, cognising atīta (past) ativibhūtarūpārammaṇa. Then, bhavaṅgacittas arise. 2.Then, samūhaggahaṇavīthi discerns the object as a whole. 3.Then, atthaggahaṇavīthi discerns the form or shape of rūpārammaṇa. 4.Then, nāmaggahaṇavīthi discerns the name of rūpārammaṇa."
