    "answer": "Gatinimiitta (sign of destiny) is a symbol of ārammaṇa (object) to be obtained and experienced in the immediately following bhava (existence). There are 2 types of gatinimitta: 1.Upalabhitabbagatinimitta ārammaṇas that will be obtained 2.Upabhogabhūtagatinimitta ārammaṇas that will become For example, for those who will be reborn in devaloka, chariots, palaces, ornaments, gardens are upalabhitabbagatinimitta; while sitting in a chariot, enjoying various places, wearing ornaments are upabhogabhūtagatinimitta."
