    "answer": "Visayappavatti means “the presentation of an object (ārammaṇa) to consciousness (citta) at one of the six doors (dvāra),” or “the occurrence of states of citta upon the presentation of ārammaṇa.” In vīthimuttacittas, there are 3 visayappavattis: kamma-ārammaṇa, kammanimitta-ārammaṇa and In vīthicittas, there are 6 visayappavattis: atimahanta-ārammaṇa, mahanta-ārammaṇa, paritta-ārammaṇa, atiparitta-ārammaṇa, vibhūta-ārammaṇa and avibhūta-ārammaṇa Or 8: atimahanta-ārammaṇa, mahanta-ārammaṇa, paritta-ārammaṇa, atiparitta-ārammaṇa, ativibhūta-ārammaṇa, vibhūta-ārammaṇa, avibhūta-ārammaṇa and ati-avibhūta-ārammaṇa"
